  "result": "Committed as `e54a8e8`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented both modules per BRIEF.md using TDD (wrote failing tests first, watched them fail, then implemented):\n\n**`src/validate.js`** — `validate({ email, password })`:\n- Missing/blank email → `Enter your email address`\n- Email without `@` → `Enter a valid email address`\n- Missing password → `Enter a password`\n- Password under 8 chars → `Use at least 8 characters`\n- Valid input → `{}`\n\n**`src/form.js`** — `render({ values, errors, submitting })`:\n- Each input has `id`/`name` and a `<label for=\"...\">`\n- Values are HTML-escaped (`&`, `<`, `>`, `\"`) in `value=\"…\"`\n- Fields with errors get `aria-invalid=\"true\"`, `aria-describedby=\"<id>-error\"`, and a following `<p id=\"<id>-error\" class=\"error\">`\n- When any errors exist, a `<div role=\"alert\" id=\"form-errors\">` with a `<ul>` of links (`<a href=\"#<id>\">`) precedes the fields; absent otherwise\n- `submitting: true` → `aria-busy=\"true\"` on the form, `disabled` button, text `Signing up…`; otherwise `Sign up`\n\n**Verification**: 15 tests across `test/validate.test.js` (6 tests) and `test/form.test.js` (9 tests), run via `npm test` — all passing. I also manually inspected `render()` output for the empty state and a combined errors+submitting state to confirm the markup matches the spec exactly."
